{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789513153,"nonce":"q8nQgFw1FIFNYV+koZ/9B7+rfCs=","title":"Python: stdlib functions imported by name were dynamic during signature inference","message":"`from math import sin` followed by `def f(i): return sin(i)` gave `f` a dynamic return type: the module built for inference carried neither the imports nor the from-names, so `sin` was an unknown name there, though the lowering typed the same call as a float. Every function returning or storing such a call was dynamic downstream; float.py's Point fields were boxes for this reason. The inference module now carries both maps.","files":null}]}